    "created_at": "2024-03-10T17:17:06Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-03-10T17:17:06Z",
    "body": "Technically what you’re saying is true, but doing so doesn’t always pan out to be a good accessible ux. \r\n\r\nMany well made SPAs use links in their navigation elements to update the primary content of the page, and then implement the necessary focus management or live region states to mimic the behavior of links. \r\n\r\nwhat you’re suggesting is absolutely possible, but if you’re using buttons and checkboxes to effectively serve as links, then you’re only doing part of what’s necessary. updating just the semantic definition of a nav doesn’t really do much to help finish the job",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
